<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sasol completes ammonia expansion project.</title>
<headline>Sasol completes ammonia expansion project.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African chemicals firm Sasol Ltd said on Tuesday it had completed a 43 million rand debottlenecking project that will expand production at its ammonia plant at Sasolburg.</p>
<p>The project will see production increase by 14 percent to 830 tons of ammonia a day.</p>
<p>Sasol said the expansion project was undertaken to meet a shortfall in the Southern African ammonia market and forecast growth in regional ammonia demand.</p>
<p>Ammonia is used as a feedstock in the production of Sasol's mining explosives, fertilisers and acrylonitrile.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
